+# [P1] CI failure masking — scheduled runs execute zero tests; `|| true` family hides real failures
+
+## Task ID
+`bridge-20261027-ci-failure-masking`
+
+## Target repository
+`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-core` (pattern likely repo-wide; tracked on the public `supremeai-open` task board per federation policy).
+
+## Severity
+**P1-high — green-but-unsafe CI.** Scheduled CI cannot produce a truthful test verdict, and the `|| true` family converts required steps into silent no-ops. Distinct from #1307/#1258 (which cover the immediate upload-sarif one-line fix); this order covers the masking family itself.
+
+## Verified evidence (pulled live via MCP tower, 2026-10-26)
+- `github_read_file {repo:"supremeai-core", path:".github/workflows/ci.yml"}` (5,414 chars):
+  - `test` job `if` includes `push || pull_request || (workflow_dispatch && !run_autofix)` — **`schedule` is excluded** → nightly runs execute **zero tests**.
+  - `autofix` job (schedule-only) wraps its steps in `|| true` (PyErrorFix scan, install steps), and the audit additionally flags `pip install -r requirements.txt || true`, empty-SARIF fallbacks, and federation watchdog `curl … || true`.
+- `github_get_failed_logs {runId:"40286008931", repo:"supremeai-core"}` → failed job **"🔧 PyErrorFix Engine"** (job name now live-confirmed; only the unguarded `github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3` step can deterministically fail — consistent with the #1307 diagnosis).
+- Cross-audit: the 2026-10-26 comprehensive audit lists CI masking as a P1 root cause ("CI green রাখার জন্য failure masking").
+
+## Why this matters
+- "Scheduled CI passes" currently carries no information: it runs no tests, and where it does run, failures are masked.
+- Release decisions inherit the lie: a repo can be simultaneously red-in-fact and green-in-CI.
+- Masked failures also corrupt automation that trusts CI (federation watchdog, PR guardian evidence).
+
+## Remediation plan
+1. Add `schedule` to the `test` job's `if` (or split a dedicated nightly test workflow) so nightly runs produce a real verdict.
+2. Remove `|| true` from every required step; where suppression is intentional, use `continue-on-error: true` + an explicit follow-up reporting step so the failure is still visible in the summary.
+3. Make SARIF upload conditional on token/permissions availability instead of letting it define the job's fate (aligns with the #1307 one-line fix).
+4. Add a CI self-test: a deliberately broken artifact must turn the workflow red (proves masking is gone).
+5. Sweep all repos' `.github/workflows/*.yml` for `|| true` on required paths; file per-repo follow-ups with counts.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] Nightly schedule executes the test suite and reports a truthful verdict
+- [ ] No `|| true` remains on required steps in core CI (or each has explicit continue-on-error + reporting)
+- [ ] Negative-control CI run demonstrates red-on-broken
+- [ ] Masking sweep report for the organization committed
+
+## Related orders
+- #1307 / #1258 — the one-line `continue-on-error` fix for the current red autofix lane (land that first; this order is the systemic follow-up)
+- Audit "SupremeAI সমন্বিত Executive Diagnosis" (2026-10-26), P1 CI items.
+
